From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:45:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: require the texel-buffer flag for PIPE_BUFFER
 sampler views

panfrost_is_format_supported() ignored the target, so a PIPE_BUFFER
sampler view or image was accepted for any texturable format, although
the format table marks the texel-buffer capable formats separately
(PAN_BIND_TEXEL_BUFFER, which panvk already checks). On Bifrost texel
buffers are read through the attribute unit, and A8_UNORM is a
texture-only format on v7: rusticl exposed CL_A/CL_UNORM_INT8 for
CL_MEM_OBJECT_IMAGE1D_BUFFER, and the OpenCL-CTS samplerless float
1Dbuffer test of that format faults the Mali-G31 with
"js fault, status=INSTR_INVALID_ENC" (the kernel is the same one every
other format runs fine with; only the attribute format differs, and v7
has no 000R component order to read an R8 attribute as alpha).

Add PAN_BIND_TEXEL_BUFFER to the requested flags for sampler views and
images on PIPE_BUFFER. On v7 this drops only A8_UNORM, RGBA4,
RGB10A2_SINT, R3G3B2 and the YUV/X6 formats from texel buffers, none of
which GL ES or Vulkan allow there; for OpenCL only CL_A/CL_UNORM_INT8
1D-buffer images go (1D/2D/3D CL_A images stay).

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_screen.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_screen.c
index 5f7c8ac1d22..9a12e832808 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_screen.c
@@ -184,6 +184,16 @@ panfrost_is_format_supported(struct pipe_screen *screen,
 
    unsigned pan_bind_flags = pipe_to_pan_bind_flags(bind);
    struct pan_format fmt = dev->formats[format];
+
+   /* Texel buffers (sampler views and images on a PIPE_BUFFER) are read
+    * through the attribute unit on Bifrost and through buffer descriptors on
+    * Valhall: only the formats marked as texel-buffer capable work there
+    * (panvk already checks this flag). A8_UNORM, for one, is a texture-only
+    * format on v7: an attribute in that format faults the G31 with
+    * INSTR_INVALID_ENC. */
+   if (target == PIPE_BUFFER &&
+       (bind & (PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW | PIPE_BIND_SHADER_IMAGE)))
+      pan_bind_flags |= PAN_BIND_TEXEL_BUFFER;
    unsigned fmt_bind_flags = fmt.bind;
 
    /* Also check that compressed texture formats are supported on this
